IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-46. NOUNS of a cross-reference. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the National Health Insurance Law, 5754-1994. It records citations: for each, what the citing words say they point at, what the target is,
-- and where each of the two readings comes from. A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same
-- thing are the same kind. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`ext:[nhi]`, `ext:[nii]` and `ext:[order]` lines are the deposited
-- Hebrew Wikisource consolidations, which are not official; `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of Sefer HaChukim and checked against its text layer;
-- `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a page image of Kovetz HaTakanot, whose PDFs have no text layer, so they are not machine-checked).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `the meaning of the term for the reduced amount`
    `a provision that fixes a sum by the average wage of the first month of a quarter`
    `the provision that fixes the reduced amount`
    `a power to fix a sum by order, with the reduced collection threshold defined in another section`
    `the chapter on insurance against injury at work`
    `the chapter on maternity insurance`
    `the chapter on disability insurance`
    `no chapter by that name in the consolidation`
    `the definition of a quarter in the schedule of highest and lowest incomes`
    `the rule that no contributions are paid for the time a person is determined to be missing`

DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the latest official instrument read, from its page image; a later change is not ruled out`
    `the official instrument for one part and the consolidation only for another`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the same letter in the 1968 numbering names` IS A MAYBE `What a provision is about`
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A change of the version cited` HAS
    `the instrument that made it` IS A STRING
    `it was published on` IS A DATE
    `the regulations in question were published on` IS A DATE
    `the version named before` IS A STRING
    `the version named after` IS A STRING

-- A day that an official instruction names twice, once by its Hebrew date and once by its Gregorian date (P4). The two dates are converted to Gregorian days with the calendar routine in NOTES.md.
DECLARE `A day given twice` HAS
    `the words giving the day are in` IS A STRING
    `the Hebrew date names` IS A DATE
    `the Gregorian date names` IS A DATE
    `the consolidation prints the same pair` IS A BOOLEAN
    `read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
